{
  "manufacturer": "Schneider Electric",
  "manufacturer_slug": "schneider-electric",
  "model": "Conext CL three-phase PV inverter 18/20/25 kVA",
  "model_slug": "conext-cl",
  "short_model": "Conext CL",
  "aliases": [
    "Conext CL-NA",
    "Conext CL-E",
    "PVSCL18NA",
    "PVSCL20E",
    "PVSCL25E",
    "PVSCL25NA"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Solar inverter",
  "applies_to": "Conext CL (IEC, PVSCL20E/25E) and Conext CL-NA (PVSCL18NA/25NA) three-phase string inverters, map revision 1.5.",
  "summary": "Schneider's Conext CL is a three-phase grid-tie string inverter with two MPPT inputs and Modbus RTU on RS-485 plus Modbus TCP. All data are holding registers in a vendor map that also embeds SunSpec models 1, 103 and 160 from 0x9C40. This map covers identity strings, lifetime energy, operating state, temperatures, grid voltages, currents, power and frequency, PV input values, the alarm code, the remote on/off command and the active-power limit.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 10,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The map prints addresses in hex and says they are 0-based ('on the wire') addresses, not 1-based. So 0x17FE (active power) is requested as 6142 decimal with no offset."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Registers Map - Conext CL Three Phase PV Inverter 20/25kVA",
    "doc_number": "503-0243-01-01 Rev 1.5",
    "revision_date": "2016-03-15",
    "url": "https://solar.se.com/au/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2021/11/Conext-CL_Modbus-Registers-Map_Rev1.5.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 5-6 (port settings, functions, addressing), 7-21 (registers), 21-23 (alarm codes)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Scaling: the map writes units as 'kW/X10', 'Vrms/X10', 'C/X10' and so on, meaning the raw value is ten times the real value (scale 0.1).",
    "Lifetime energy 0x0802-0x0803 is the only 32-bit value whose high and low words the map labels (H word first), so it is listed as ABCD. The other 32-bit registers (daily energy 0x0804-0x0811, operating hours 0x081E, event codes, the UTC clock at 0x1920 and the SunSpec acc32 energy at 0x9C9E) carry no word-order statement and are left out.",
    "0x1700 and the SunSpec vendor status 0x9CAD state their codes in hex: 15h = 21, 16h = 22, 17h = 23 decimal.",
    "Remote command 0xEFFE and inverter mode 0xFA90 take the hex command words 6B42-6B45; they are listed in decimal under values (0x6B42 = 27458).",
    "Section 4 of the map lists the alarm codes reported in 0x1828 (e.g. 2450 No-Grid, 2616 PV insulation, 4003 Replace fan); they are not repeated here.",
    "Not listed: software part/build/checksum strings, event logs with time stamps (0x1900-0x193F), the rest of the SunSpec blocks and the reactive-power, LVRT and multifunction-relay settings. Several reactive power and LVRT registers are marked 'Not available' in this revision.",
    "Unused addresses return 0xFF bytes rather than an exception."
  ],
